{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Controlling the Story"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Cycle"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe rules through a  wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le09ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Infinitives of Purpose"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Explaining how to do something means using verbs for the actions that must be carried out. These are called infinitives of purpose."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure: </br><span class=\"italic\">verb </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">Infinitive</span> </br> to explain why you do something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Infinitives of purpose answer the question \u201cWhy?\u201d. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We want to learn through mistakes <span class=\"underline\">to avoid</span> similar problems in the future.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here, you can ask the question \u201cWhy?\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We want to learn through mistakes.  </br>Why? </br>To avoid similar problems in the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A quick and appropriate response for damage control is necessary <span class=\"underline\">to prevent</span> the problem from getting worse"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Fourth, a solution must be made <span class=\"underline\">to deal with</span> the problem. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It enables us <span class=\"underline\">to manage</span> small challenges before they become bigger ones. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "And so we come back around to the first step in preparing <span class=\"underline\">to avert</span> the next crisis."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Organizing Points in an Argument"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " While numbering points is one clear way to organize an argument, there are various ways of wording a sequence of steps. Using the same wording for each step may sound stiff or unnatural so a variety of sentence structures are often used."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look for the clue in each sentence which shows which stage of the argument you are reading."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Variations:</span><span class=\"italic\"></br>First, ... </br>The first step / thing / stage ... </br>This is step / number / level / one. </br>Moving to step two, ... </br>Then,\u2026</br>This leads us the second idea ... </br>... and move to step two: </br>And third ... </br>After that, \u2026 </br>And finally ... </br>*</span>Note: \u2018And' is only used to precede the last step or idea."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">The first step</span> to keeping a house clean is to prevent it from getting dirty. For instance, you might remove your shoes before entering a room. But sometimes you notice that dirt has gathered anyway. This is <span class=\"underline\">the second step:</span> seeing the need to clean. We notice the problem and <span class=\"underline\">move to step three</span>: responding immediately. Stop whatever it is you were doing to attend to the mess. Fourth, analyze the situation. What supplies are needed for cleaning? And finally, just get dirty and do your cleaning!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "avoidable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "possible to stay away from; preventable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many avoidable crises occur because preparation has not been done. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le09ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to do research in crisis management."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to detect "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to notice something that is not obvious"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is the second step, the stage of detection."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le09ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "immediately "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "right away"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We respond immediately and move to step three."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le09ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "containment "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the action of keeping something harmful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Step three is containment of the problem."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le09ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "damage control "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "action taken to limit the harmful effects of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is important to prevent the problem from getting worse so a quick and appropriate response for damage control is necessary."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le09ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine a task at work that needs doing and write it down."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down any steps that need to be done in point form, using infinitives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange your task with your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Order each other's steps with variety."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your tasks aloud to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I plan what things need to be done for a task."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present tasks that need doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use a variety of language techniques to order a work mate's plan of action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my plans aloud to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can use language techniques to organize points in an argument."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about goals and purposes."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Is a small crisis much easier to deal with than a big one?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How does dealing with small crises prepare you for bigger ones?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask Your Partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Each online article has a different approach."}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">First things first</span>."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content"